VCVT2PS2PHX never set its MXCSR flags

AVX10.2 spec, VCVT2PS2PHX: the instruction "updates MXCSR as if all MXCSR
numerical exceptions flags are masked and does not generate floating point
exceptions", and can set DE, IE, OE, PE and UE. The handler set
softfloat_suppressException to every flag, so softfloat_getExceptionFlags()
always returned 0 and MXCSR never changed: vcvt2ps2phx of 1/3 left PE clear
where vcvtps2phx sets it.

Dropping the suppression alone is not enough: check_exceptionsSSE() judges
masking by MXCSR, so with an exception unmasked there it would raise #XM.
The flags are now ORed into MXCSR directly.

Fixed in avx/avx10_2_cvt.cc. Found 2026-09-29 while auditing the FP16
handlers' MXCSR handling.

diff --git a/cpu/avx/avx10_2_cvt.cc b/cpu/avx/avx10_2_cvt.cc
index 63beb61..1564a22 100644
--- a/cpu/avx/avx10_2_cvt.cc
+++ b/cpu/avx/avx10_2_cvt.cc
@@ -47,7 +47,6 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::VCVT2PS2PHX_MASK_VphHpsWpsR(bxInstruction_
   softfloat_status_word_rc_override(status, i);
   status.softfloat_flush_underflow_to_zero = 0; // ignore MXCSR.FUZ
   status.softfloat_exceptionMasks = softfloat_all_exceptions_mask;
-  status.softfloat_suppressException = softfloat_all_exceptions_mask;
 
   Bit32u mask, opmask = i->opmask() ? BX_READ_32BIT_OPMASK(i->opmask()) : (Bit32u) -1;
 
@@ -67,7 +66,8 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::VCVT2PS2PHX_MASK_VphHpsWpsR(bxInstruction_
       dst.vmm16u(n + num_elements_from_source) = 0;
   }
 
-  check_exceptionsSSE(softfloat_getExceptionFlags(&status));
+  // not check_exceptionsSSE(): it would raise #XM for an exception unmasked in MXCSR
+  MXCSR.set_exceptions(softfloat_getExceptionFlags(&status));
 
   BX_WRITE_AVX_REGZ(i->dst(), dst, len);
   BX_NEXT_INSTR(i);
